-- title:
--   Invariant element of Jⁿ generating Jⁿ at every end
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$ and $M'$ a positive natural number with $q \nmid M'$; let $\ell$ be a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which (`hK`) is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(N_0)$, where $N_0 = (q\ell)^2 M'$ and $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$ on units.
--
--   **Base ring and chart.** Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-algebra-domain with $L$ as its fraction field and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent series is the coefficient image of the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function (`hj`), let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q \cdot (\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`). Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point over $\Omega$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$: the existence of a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to seven clauses (summarised here): $e$ carries germs of constants $a \in A$ to $C(\sigma a)$; the level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K/L$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ — those satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) N₀ H γ⁻¹ K τ`, i.e. for all weights, all modular forms $f_1,g_1$ of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions and all $x \in K$ representing $f_1/g_1$, the series of $\tau x$ reads complex-analytically as $(f_1/g_1)$ twisted by the matrix attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ and the level $q\ell$ — preserve $C$; those with $\gamma$ also in $\Gamma(\ell)$ fix $y'$ pointwise modulo $y'$; every such $\tau$ fixing $y'$ pointwise modulo $y'$ induces an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ compatible with $e$ and the germ map, fixing constants, acting on $X_0,X_1$ through a matrix $M$ over $W$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, with a scalar $c$ satisfying $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M \equiv c\,\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ avoiding $(X_0,X_1)$, containing $\sigma\varpi$ and containing linear forms with integral coefficients $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ contract to distinct ideals of the stalk whenever $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; for such a prime containing $X_0$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ lies in its contraction to the stalk exactly when all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lie in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and the element `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` (the $j$-expansion in the parameter of level $q\ell$) lies in $C$, and after subtraction of a suitable $a_0 \in A$ it is carried by $e$ to a class $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b)$ in $W$, not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **The linked frame.** Fixed in addition are: a point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'$ equal to $y$ (`hy'y`); and one explicit witness of the above data at $z$: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this witness the same seven clauses listed above (constants, preservation of $C$, triviality modulo $y'$ on $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$, the equivariance clause with $\theta$, $c$, $M$, the separation of branches, the coefficient criterion for a branch, and the Hasse-type clause on `jqNModC`).
--
--   **The centre, the blow-up chart and the valuation ring.** Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau|_C^{-1}\bigl((e_1 \circ \text{completion} \circ \text{germ})^{-1}(\,(\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\,X_0,\,X_1\,)\,)\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ that preserve $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and assume: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$; `hR2`, that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ precisely when $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ outside $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W$, through an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}(\gamma), c)$ in the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$ acting by `hAction`, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that the level automorphisms for $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the target of $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ carried into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The ends.** Let `ends` be a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised by `hends` as follows: a subring $O$ belongs to it exactly when there is a nonzero $a \in J$ such that, putting $B_a$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : xa \in J\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ equal to the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (i.e. $f \in O$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$), such that every element of $y$ that lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B \not\subseteq O$. Finally `hperm` asserts that the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserve $W$ permute `ends`: for each $O$ in `ends` there is $O'$ in `ends` with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$ for all $f \in K$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a natural number $n$ and an element $S$ of $C$ such that $1 \le n$, $S \in J^n$, $S \neq 0$ in $K$, and
--
--   (i) $\tau(S) = S$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ (in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt` with the parameters above);
--
--   (ii) for every $O$ in `ends` and every $i \in J^n$, the element $i \cdot S^{-1}$ of $K$ lies in $O$.
--
--   This is the geometric input for the construction of a common chart on the blow-up of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ along the weighted centre $J$ at a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$: an invariant element of some power $J^n$ which generates $J^n$ in the local ring of every end of the blow-up. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), and its proof invokes the finiteness of the group of level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, the stability of the centre under those automorphisms, and the existence of a finite family of sections dominating the weighted centre at the ends.
